# kill.log -- userspace transcripts of the 2026-09-14 / 09-15 root runs
#
# DEVICE   OPPO Find X5 Pro (PFEM10), SM8450, ColorOS 16.0.3.520 (CN01)
# KERNEL   5.10.236-android12-9-o-gaf2075ad2c06
# BOOT     bootloader locked, green
# SOURCE   adb shell stdout of the exploit, tee'd to /data/local/tmp/ and
#          pulled. Reproduced verbatim, not edited.
#
# WHAT IS HERE
#   RUN 1/2  full chain to uid=0 + kernelsu.ko loaded. 2026-09-14.
#   RUN 3    same chain plus the "crowning test": the KernelSU manager was
#            launched and polled for 120 s. THIS IS THE MOST INFORMATIVE RUN --
#            the manager survived and the module stayed loaded, i.e. in this run
#            nothing killed anything. 2026-09-14.
#   RUN 4    the 2026-09-15 attempt: same chain, ksud loaded via memfd, and
#            afterwards the Android framework services were gone
#            ("Can't find service: package/power/input/phone/wifi") while the
#            kernelsu module was still Live. Device needed a manual reboot.
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE  (read before drawing conclusions)
#   * No dmesg / logcat-kernel excerpt for any of these runs.
#       - `dmesg` is `klogctl: Permission denied` while SELinux is Enforcing.
#         These runs flip to Permissive via the W1 stage *inside* the run, and
#         dmesg was never read back afterwards.  A dmesg capture from a
#         different boot does exist (see notes.md sec.6) and contains no
#         [ROOTCHECK-*] line at all.
#       - `logcat -b kernel` was tried (`tools/phase1_capture.sh`) and returns
#         an empty buffer on this device.
#     So there is NO `[ROOTCHECK-*]` text and NO
#     `$$sys_call_number@@ / $$set_id_flag@@ / $$addr_limit@@ / $$enforce@@`
#     payload anywhere below.  That payload goes to a userspace daemon through
#     kevent_send_to_user, not to the console.
#   * Nothing below proves WHY anything stopped.  It proves that uid=0 was
#     reached, that kernelsu.ko loaded, and -- in RUN 3 -- that the module and
#     the manager were both still alive 120 s later.
#
# HOW TO CLOSE THE GAP  (full recipe in evidence/notes.md sec.6)
#   1. reach Permissive first (W1 stage of the same run)
#   2. keep `dmesg -w | grep -E 'ROOTCHECK|oplus_root'` running into
#      /data/local/tmp/k for the whole run
#   3. pull /data/local/tmp/k afterwards
#

